    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft-duplicate detection for `POST /api/owners`: when a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a different telephone, it's still created and the response now reports `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id (otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor conventions (one small cohesive function class per step), the change is spread across small units rather than growing any existing function:\n\n- **`DetectPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new) \u2014 a single small step that, given the built `@Val Owner` and the repository, records the matching existing owner's id via `owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(...)`. Mirrors the existing `CountNamesakes`/`RequireUniqueHousehold` pattern.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step between `namesakes` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 one persisted field `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) plus its getter/setter; the boolean `possibleDuplicate` is derived, not stored.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` expression deriving `possibleDuplicate` as `getPossibleDuplicateOf() != null`; `possibleDuplicateOf` auto-maps by name.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO exposes them.\n- **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`data.sql`** \u2014 added the `possible_duplicate_of` column (appended last to keep positional seed inserts aligned; I only touched the hsqldb schema, matching how `namesake_count`/`postcode` were previously maintained).\n\nDesign choices that kept structural impact low: I persisted a single nullable `Integer` (deriving the boolean in the mapper) rather than two columns/accessors, and I added a new tiny step instead of enlarging `CountNamesakes` \u2014 so every changed function stays at CC ~1\u20133 with minimal surrounding complexity. The new `AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` and the full suite pass (BUILD SUCCESS).",
